6. THE INTERACTION WITH L4-E5 (R10 115k to 232k, the ceiling raised, C26 and C27 re-rated)
   apply_gen_sch_e_hold.py: 1 edit(s); names R10: no; R10's drawn line still present once after it: yes; carries C861068, C728597: yes
   apply_gen_sch_e_input_limit.py: 9 edit(s); names R10: no; R10's drawn line still present once after it: yes; carries C2903494, C861244, C14663: yes
   apply_gen_sch_e_u5_grade.py: 2 edit(s); names R10: no; R10's drawn line still present once after it: yes; carries C674169: yes
   U5's junction is taken at L4-E5's raised EXTVCC (30.15 V): 105.4 C; the stage's input stays at or under REQ-016's window, so
   L4-E5's line (sized for the window's 100 W) covers it; the hold and the limit are on the input, R10 and C26/C27 on the output

7. INCONCLUSIVE (no printed bound), each with the measurement that bounds it
   - EA2's voltage gain (130 V/V TYP, p.5) and VC's operating range: the corner passes for an EA2 gain at or above 25.026426 V/V
     cold and 24.924212 V/V hot under stack A, and 55.191656 V/V cold and 54.709122 V/V hot with stack C's other terms (line x2, drifts).
     Bench: in input-current limit at 25 V, step the load to move VC across its range, read VC and IMON_IN; the gain is
     dVC / dV(IMON_IN); accept at or above 65 V/V (the floor), and at least the break-even at every point
   - the IMON_IN reference's line regulation while switching and at both ends (printed at 25 C, not switching, p.4): the corner
     passes up to 62 times its printed maximum (stack A, cold end). Bench: the limit's current at VIN 16 and 25 V, switching,
     at both ends
   - RSENSE1's TCR below +25 C (HoJLR p.4 tests +25 to +125 C): passes up to 882 ppm/K (stack A) and 122 ppm/K (stack C). Bench: R59 at -20 C
     and +25 C
   - EA3's gain (90 V/V TYP) and the FBIN bias (10 nA TYP): no compliance effect (the corner is at 25 V); an energy sensitivity
     only (section 5); the bench reads the hold at both ends (7b.12)
   - U5's junction (INFERRED from the gate charge at 10 V and theta-JA): the CLKOUT duty cycle method of p.34 (+-10 C)
   - the candidate panel's own source compliance (O-1) and every efficiency (C-8): unchanged by this record

8. BENCH ROWS
   7b.9 (steady state): a PV emulator puts the loaded input at the limit from 16.420 V (the kept hold's lowest: EA3 at half, the
     resistors' drifts) to 25 V, at the load's maximum, cold-soaked
     at -20 C and in 62.1 C air; V_in x I_in at or under 100 W at every point; the limit's current at 25 V at most 4.000 A
   7b.9t (transients, recorded apart): a source step (open circuit to the limit) and irradiance steps to the two panel
     scenarios of section 9 (110.2 W, a warmed 13.8 C cell; 122.7 W, a cold-soaked -20 C cell; both at 1000 W/m2); the peak and
     the time above 100 W against the filter's 2.32 ms (SESSION: no fault trip, IMON_IN under 1.55 V; above 100 W no longer
     than five time constants, 11.6 ms)
   7b.10 the EA2 gain row and 7b.11 the line row above; 7b.12 the hold, read at both ends: accepted inside 16.420 to 18.813 V (EA3 at
     half, the resistors' drifts: the conditioned envelope); a reading outside 16.970 to 18.221 V (EA3 typical, new parts) is recorded
     with EA3's gain it implies
   7b.13 U5's junction by CLKOUT at all four switches, EXTVCC at the ceiling, 62.1 C air: at most 125 C less p.34's 10 C
   7b.14 R59 at -20 C and +25 C (a design check of the cold TCR; Milliohm's statement is the qualification)

9. QUALIFICATION OF THE 100 W BOUND (the owner's instruction of 1 October 2026)
   THE SHEET: https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/8705af.pdf, read as the Internet
     Archive's snapshot 20250322064938 (the id_ form; the live site resets this runner's connection), sha256
     8f552a0b57677bfa7e4a5d5d0fac56d56fbbd1a6f65a9ee7aaaf8743cd534ec3, byte-identical to the held
     v2/vendor/power/lt8705a.pdf; it prints its document code 8705af on each of its 44 pages and carries no revision table.
     Only its rows are used
   THE CLASSIFICATION (Y: the value can move that outcome; small: it moves it by the stated fraction, nonzero; the reasons below):
     id   unprinted value                                                            bound  stability protection other
     EA2  EA2's gain and VC's operating range                                        Y      Y         N          energy, only in hours the limit binds
     A7   A7's gain outside its test point (50 mV differential, CSPIN at 5.025 V)    Y      Y         Y          energy, only in hours the limit binds
     LINE the IMON_IN reference's line regulation while switching and at temperature Y      small     N          energy, a fraction of a percent of the limit, only in hours it binds
     TCR  RSENSE1's TCR below +25 C                                                  Y      small     small      energy, a fraction of a percent of the limit, only in hours it binds
     HOLD EA3's gain and the FBIN bias                                               N      Y         N          energy (the hold band)
     TJ   U5's junction temperature                                                  Y      N         Y          lifetime (Note 3: derated above 125 C)
   EA2, EA2's gain and VC's operating range
     - the bound: the regulated IMON_IN moves by (VC - 1.2 V) / gain (p.5, p.2): 96.2474 W at 130 V/V against 95.2909 W with
       the term left out (stack A, cold)
     - loop stability: EA2 drives VC through the compensation network in the input-current loop; with no printed minimum gain
       or gm the loop's margin is not guaranteed (p.33: the loop stability is affected by a number of factors)
     - protection: the IMON_IN fault is a comparator on IMON_IN itself (p.5, 1.55 V minimum, full range), not through EA2;
       only a gain under 4.68 V/V would hold the regulated point at the fault, which stops switching (the safe side)
     - the sheet: p.5 EA2 gain 130 V/V and gm 185 umho, typical only; p.4 the IMON_IN regulation, full range, printed at VC =
       1.2 V; p.2 VC's absolute maximum -0.3 to 2.2 V; p.7 'Inductor Current Sense Voltage at Minimum Duty Cycle' against VC
       and p.8 'Maximum VC vs SS' plot VC within 0.5 to 2.0 V (TYPICAL, TA = 25 C; not a limit); p.31 the current-limiting
       text names 1.208 V typical and no gain bound
     - guaranteed limit: none printed
     - conservative assumption: EA2 at least 65 V/V (half its typical) with VC anywhere in its absolute maximum range (the
       replay's allowance doubled)
     - qualification needed: Analog Devices: EA2's minimum gain, or the IMON_IN regulation point's shift with VC, over -40 to
       125 C junction, as a limit the manufacturer warrants, with the conditions it applies to; characterization over
       production lots is supporting evidence, not a production guarantee, and the row stays CONDITIONAL until a warranted
       limit exists; a bench reading of a few units (7b.10) checks the design only
     - margin kept: 2.8579 W under its conservative assumption alone (stack A otherwise, cold end); break-even 25.026426 V/V
       (stack A, cold), 55.191656 V/V (stack C's other terms, cold)
   A7, A7's gain outside its test point (50 mV differential, CSPIN at 5.025 V)
     - the bound: the limit is 1.208 V / (gm x RSENSE1 x RIMON_IN) (p.31): the effective gain enters in proportion. The full-
       range gm row (0.94 / 1.06 mmho, E and I) is printed at a 50 mV differential with CSPIN at 5.025 V; the design runs
       CSPIN at the panel voltage, 16.420 to 25 V, and up to 57.5 mV across RSENSE1. The CSPIN and CSNIN ranges, 1.5 to 80 V
       common mode and -100 to 100 mV differential (p.5), are operating ranges, not a gain guarantee
     - loop stability: the sense path's gain enters the input-current loop in proportion; an error outside the test point
       moves the loop gain by the same fraction
     - protection: the fault comparator's threshold voltage on IMON_IN (p.5) does not move; the input current at which it
       trips moves inversely with the effective gain, as the limit does
     - the sheet: p.5 A7 gm 0.95 / 1.05 mmho at 25 C and 0.94 / 1.06 mmho over the full range (E, I), each at VCSPIN - VCSNIN
       = 50 mV and VCSPIN = 5.025 V; p.5 CSPIN and CSNIN 1.5 to 80 V common mode and -100 to 100 mV differential (operating
       ranges); p.8 'IMON Output Currents' plots the output current against the differential only (TYPICAL, TA = 25 C); no
       curve against common mode, no transfer-error or offset row
     - guaranteed limit: the gm limits at the test point, over the full temperature range; nothing printed at the design's
       common mode and differential, or while switching
     - conservative assumption: the test-point limits apply at the design's common mode and differential while switching (an
       extrapolation, ASSUMPTION)
     - qualification needed: Analog Devices: A7's transfer error (gm and offset) over the common mode, the differential, -40
       to 125 C junction and switching the design uses, as a limit the manufacturer warrants, with the conditions it applies
       to; characterization over production lots is supporting evidence, not a production guarantee, and the row stays
       CONDITIONAL until a warranted limit exists
     - margin kept: 3.7526 W under its conservative assumption alone (stack A otherwise, cold end); break-even the effective
       gain may fall to 0.904726 mmho (3.7526 % under 0.94) under stack A, 0.936935 mmho (0.3261 %) under stack C and
       0.939053 mmho (0.1008 %) under every conservative assumption together, other terms fixed (cold)
   LINE, the IMON_IN reference's line regulation while switching and at temperature
     - the bound: the reference moves with VIN from the 12 V it is printed at: at 25 V the printed maximum moves the corner
       by 0.0619 W
     - loop stability: small, not zero: the reference's VIN dependence couples a moving source voltage into the regulated
       current (a feedforward path, at most 0.0100 % of the setpoint per volt assumed), with no gain of its own; the loop's
       margin is set elsewhere
     - protection: the regulated point would reach the IMON_IN fault minimum only at 402 times the printed maximum
     - the sheet: p.4 0.002 / 0.005 %/V, VIN 12 to 80 V, not switching, at 25 C (no bullet); p.4 the regulation itself is a
       full-range row at VIN = 12 V, so its temperature drift at 12 V is guaranteed; p.7 'Feedback Voltages' against
       temperature at VC = 1.2 V is TYPICAL
     - guaranteed limit: the full-range IMON_IN regulation row covers temperature at VIN = 12 V; the VIN dependence while
       switching and away from 25 C is not printed
     - conservative assumption: twice the printed maximum (0.010 %/V), either sign, at every temperature and while switching
     - qualification needed: Analog Devices: the IMON_IN reference's line regulation while switching, over -40 to 125 C
       junction, as a limit the manufacturer warrants, with the conditions it applies to; characterization over production
       lots is supporting evidence, not a production guarantee, and the row stays CONDITIONAL until a warranted limit exists
     - small effect on loop stability: the setpoint moves with the source voltage: over the envelope's 8.580 V swing at most
       0.0429 % printed, 0.0858 % assumed
     - margin kept: 3.6906 W under its conservative assumption alone (stack A otherwise, cold end); break-even 61.6 times the
       printed maximum (stack A, cold); 47.1 with EA2 at 65 V/V
   TCR, RSENSE1's TCR below +25 C
     - the bound: RSENSE1 sits in the limit's denominator; at -20 C its TCR sets its low end
     - loop stability: small, not zero: the sense-path loop gain is proportional to RSENSE1, -0.2255 % from 50 to 100 ppm/K
       at -20 C; the loop's margin is set by the compensation
     - protection: small, not zero: the fault comparator's threshold voltage (IMON_IN 1.55 / 1.61 / 1.67 V, p.5) does not
       move, but the input current at which it trips is proportional to 1 / RSENSE1 (p.31), +0.2260 % from 50 to 100 ppm/K at
       -20 C. The fault-to-limit ratio does not depend on RSENSE1; at its least it is 1.248653 (stack A, regulation at most
       1.241337312 V) and 1.236365 with every conservative assumption (regulation at most 1.253674623 V)
     - the sheet: HoJLR2512 Ho-A0 p.2 +-50 ppm/K (2 to 500 mOhm); p.4 the TCR test spans +25 to +125 C only; the catalogue
       prints no TCR for C2903494
     - guaranteed limit: none printed
     - conservative assumption: +-100 ppm/K below +25 C (twice the printed hot-side value)
     - qualification needed: Milliohm: the HoJLR2512 TCR from -40 to +25 C, as a limit the manufacturer warrants, with the
       conditions it applies to; characterization over production lots is supporting evidence, not a production guarantee,
       and the row stays CONDITIONAL until a warranted limit exists; a bench reading of R59 at -20 C (7b.14) checks the
       design only
     - small effect on loop stability: the sense-path loop gain moves with RSENSE1: -0.2255 % from 50 to 100 ppm/K at -20 C
     - small effect on protection: the current at which the fault trips moves with 1 / RSENSE1 (p.31): +0.2260 % from 50 to
       100 ppm/K at -20 C; the comparator's threshold does not move
     - margin kept: 3.5350 W under its conservative assumption alone (stack A otherwise, cold end); break-even 882.027 ppm/K
       (stack A), 122.295 ppm/K (stack C)
   HOLD, EA3's gain and the FBIN bias
     - the bound: they set the hold, the envelope's low end 16.419845 V, where the matching stacks (each resistor at its
       worst end) read 63.1883 W (A), 65.4106 W (C, drifts included) and 65.5580 W (every conservative assumption) against
       96.2474 W, 99.6739 W and 99.8992 W at 25 V: the power rises with the input voltage at every vertex
     - loop stability: EA3 closes the input-voltage loop through VC; its margin is part of the hold's bench row
     - protection: the hold is a regulation, not a protection; FBOUT's overvoltage and the IMON_IN fault are other pins
     - the sheet: p.4 EA3 90 V/V and FBIN bias 10 nA, typical only; p.4 FBIN regulation 1.184 / 1.226 V, full range (I
       grade), at VC = 1.2 V
     - guaranteed limit: the FBIN reference is full range; the gain and the bias are typical
     - conservative assumption: EA3 at half its typical with the resistors' drifts: the hold inside 16.420 to 18.813 V; the
       bias at ten times its typical moves the lower corner by -9.2 mV
     - qualification needed: none for the bound; the hold's energy rows carry them as sensitivities and 7b.12 reads the hold
   TJ, U5's junction temperature
     - the bound: every LT8705A row the corner uses is a full-range row, guaranteed for the I grade from -40 to 125 C
       junction (p.6 Note 3); the bound needs only the junction inside that range, not its value
     - loop stability: the loop's gains move with temperature inside the unprinted EA2 and A7 rows already carried above
     - protection: the overtemperature protection acts at approximately 165 C (p.34, approximate): the estimate stays 59.6 K
       under it
     - the sheet: p.2 theta-JA 34 C/W (UHF, a package figure on the maker's board); p.3 the VIN quiescent current, 4.2 mA
       maximum, printed at 25 C, not switching, EXTVCC = 0; p.6 Note 3 and Note 8; p.34 the CLKOUT method (+-10 C) and the
       thermal shutdown at approximately 165 C
     - guaranteed limit: the I grade's rows hold over -40 to 125 C junction; no junction temperature is printed for this
       board
     - conservative assumption: an INFERRED estimate, TJ about 105.4 C: the maximum gate charge at 10 V for all four FETs at
       the highest oscillator frequency, the VIN quiescent maximum (printed at 25 C, not switching, EXTVCC = 0, so an
       extrapolation), EXTVCC at L4-E5's 30.15 V ceiling and theta-JA 34 C/W (board-dependent) in 62.1 C air; not a
       demonstrated upper bound
     - qualification needed: a design verification of board E's thermal path (7b.13 by p.34's method, +-10 C), with the
       margin covering the unit spread the maximum gate charge already bounds
     - margin kept: 19.6 K of junction; break-even 125 C junction (19.6 K above the estimate)
   THE RESULT: CONDITIONAL on EA2, A7, LINE, TCR, TJ. 96.2474 W (cold) and 96.2291 W (hot), 96.2481 W with each resistor
   at its own worst end (the mixed envelope), are calculated results under the assumptions listed below. Under each
   unresolved row's conservative assumption alone the cold corner reads 97.1421 / 96.3094 / 96.4650 W (EA2 / LINE / TCR);
   A7 at its test-point limits is stack A itself, and TJ moves no figure while the junction stays inside -40 to 125 C.
   All of them together with the resistors' drifts read 99.8992 W (stack C with RSENSE1's cold TCR at 100 ppm/K): margin
   0.1008 W, which A7 consumes at an effective gain 0.1008 % under its printed minimum (0.939053 mmho). The design floor
   stack C itself reads 99.6739 / 99.6549 W (cold / hot)
   THE ASSUMPTIONS OF 96.25 W (stack A), in one list:
     1. 8705af's full-range rows for the I grade: the IMON_IN regulation 1.187 / 1.229 V and A7's gm 0.94 / 1.06 mmho,
        with U5's junction inside -40 to 125 C (an INFERRED estimate of about 105.4 C, not a demonstrated bound)
     2. A7's gm limits, printed at VCSPIN - VCSNIN = 50 mV and VCSPIN = 5.025 V, applied at the design's common mode
        16.420 to 25 V and up to 57.5 mV differential while switching (ASSUMPTION, condition A7)
     3. the IMON_IN line regulation at its printed maximum (0.005 %/V, 25 C, not switching), applied while switching and
        at both ends (ASSUMPTION)
     4. EA2's gain at its typical 130 V/V as its bound, with VC anywhere in its absolute maximum range -0.3 to 2.2 V
        (ASSUMPTION)
     5. RSENSE1 15 mOhm +-1 % and +-50 ppm/K, the TCR printed for +25 to +125 C applied at -20 C (ASSUMPTION); its hot end
        70.1 C by the derating line (INFERRED)
     6. RIMON_IN 23.2k +-0.1 %, +-25 ppm/K (tested from -55 to +125 C); the resistors' soldering and life drifts not
        stacked (they are in C and D)
     7. both resistors in the same inside air at each end (the thermal coupling of the paired ends); the mixed envelope
        below drops it
     8. the envelope: the input from the hold's lowest 16.420 V to REQ-016's 25 V, ambient -20 to +40 C (REQ-024), inside
        air at most 62.1 C (pcb_envelope.yaml)
     9. nothing in series with CSPIN or CSNIN (p.30): R59's pads are their Kelvin taps (a layout obligation)
     10. steady state; transients are 7b.9t's
     11. the setting realised as drafted: R59 15 mOhm and R16 23.2k with C65 (the drafts applied in a circuit round)
   WHY THE CORNERS BOUND THE PERMITTED RANGE
     - the input voltage: P = v x I_set x [Vref (1 + ls lam (v - 12)) + es dVC / G] / (Vref_typ gm r1 r2); its slope in v is
       I_set [Vref (1 + ls lam (2v - 12)) + es dVC / G] / (Vref_typ gm r1 r2), whose bracket is at least 1.173206 V (stack A) and
       1.159412 V (stack C) at every vertex over 16.420 to 25 V: the power rises with v, so 25 V is the worst; no loaded voltage
       exceeds REQ-016's 25 V open circuit (the panel is PV_P's only source and in discontinuous mode M4 is held off on reverse
       current, p.18); the hold's lowest is the floor (there, with matching stacks and each resistor at its worst end: 63.1883 W
       A, 65.4106 W C with the drifts, 65.5580 W with every conservative assumption). The dense check (0.01 V) of each stack finds
       its worst at the 25 V vertex
     - every tolerance direction: P is monotonic in each term (up in Vref, in the line term for v above 12 V, in the EA2 term;
       down in gm, RSENSE1 and RIMON_IN), so the 64 vertices an end hold the extremes; a resistor's low end 1 - a|T - 25| is
       least at the end of its temperature span farthest from 25 C, so the two ends are enough
     - temperature: the air from -20 C (no self-heating; self-heating only moves a part toward 25 C there) to 62.1 C plus
       RSENSE1's own rise (70.1 C); the LT8705A rows are full range, so U5's junction enters only as the condition -40 to
       125 C. RSENSE1 would have to reach past its 170 C rating (stack A) or 139.0 C (stack C) for the corner to reach 100 W:
       a board hot spot beside L1 and the FETs is covered by that much
     - the thermal coupling: the paired ends assume both resistors sit in the same inside air at each end (RSENSE1 adds its
       own rise). The mixed envelope drops that and lets each take its own worst end: 96.248120559 W (A), 99.674651953 W
       (C), 99.899220557 W (every conservative assumption), against 96.247433497 / 99.673940430 / 99.899220557 W paired; a
       dense air sweep from -20 to 62.1 C in 0.1 C steps, RSENSE1 with and without its rise, finds 96.247433497 /
       99.673940430 / 99.899220557 W. The mixed envelope is the bound's figure
   STATES OUTSIDE THE CORNERS
     - below -20 C ambient: outside REQ-024's -20 to +40 C. Computed for information at -40 C (the I grade's least junction):
       the candidate's open circuit reaches 25.23 V there, outside REQ-016's window; the corner at that voltage with both
       resistors at -40 C reads 97.2744 W under stack A
     - a source step (a panel plugged in live): TRK_VIN's 224.8 uF (NETLIST: C11, C12, C13, C14, C15, C64) charge through R59 at
       most the panel's short circuit, 70.2 mJ at 25 V; start-up ramps VC by the soft start (p.15). Bench 7b.9t
     - an irradiance step, two scenarios of the candidate panel (100 W +6 %, -0.35 %/K, 1000 W/m2; INFERRED from its sheet):
       110.2 W with a cell warmed to 13.8 C by the NOCT model in -20 C air, and 122.7 W with a cold-soaked -20 C cell; either
       exceeds 100 W until the IMON_IN loop settles through CIMON_IN (tau 2.32 ms). Bench 7b.9t, both scenarios
     - the hold transition: VC passes between EA3 and EA2 (the diode-AND, p.14); each side's steady state is bounded above.
       The handover is a transient: bench 7b.9t
     - an unstable current loop would break the steady-state premise: bench 7b.9t with p.33's load and line steps
   THE DESIGN OPTION THAT REMOVES AN UNKNOWN (SESSION decision): RSENSE1's cold TCR. Of the stocked 15 mOhm 1 % 2512
     parts read, only Vishay Dale's WSL2512 (WSL2512R0150FEA, LCSC C844695, stock 13410; Document 30100, Revision
     23-Nov-2023, p.2) states its TCR from -55 C: +-75 ppm/K, 1.0 W at 70 C (HoJLR: +25 to +125 C, Ho-A0 p.4; YAGEO PA V.10
     p.9 and RALEC LR IE-SP-060 p.10: the hot side only). Its printed solder-heat and life limits each carry 0.5 mOhm
     (p.3): 3.83 % and 4.33 % of 15 mOhm. With it, stack A reads 96.4763 W (RSENSE1 at 89.2 C by 100 K/W, INFERRED) and the
     design floor 106.9760 W at 23.2k; the same rule would move RIMON_IN to 24.9k (3.2343 A), 6.8 % less input in every
     hour the limit binds
     NOT TAKEN: the swap trades an unknown with a large margin (break-even 122.295 ppm/K under stack C, 2.4 times the
     printed value) for a certain loss of setting; the unknown is qualified by Milliohm's statement instead
     (clarification/)
   CLARIFICATION REQUESTS (text for the owner to send; the session contacts no one): clarification/analog-devices-lt8705a.txt,
     clarification/milliohm-hojlr2512.txt
   PROTOTYPE MEASUREMENTS ARE DOWNSTREAM OBLIGATIONS, NOT BLOCKERS: no architecture decision depends on 7b.9, 7b.9t, 7b.10,
     7b.11, 7b.12, 7b.13 or 7b.14 (R59 at -20 C and +25 C). The current-limit mechanism holds its bound under the conservative
     assumptions above; an adverse reading changes a value (RIMON_IN, the compensation), not the mechanism or the architecture
